(A walk over a buffer reads it as it is at every byte: growth in the body,
 which can move the buffer, and `Free`, which ends the walk.)
a buffer called hold is "abc".
For each b in hold, print b, append "abcdefgh" to hold, append "abcdefgh" to hold.
Print "size: {hold's size}".
a buffer called gone is "xyz".
For each b in gone, print b, Free gone.
Print "gone: {gone's size}".
